# Examples and Use Cases
Every project and every customer's site is a little bit different. And any engineer who designs an infrastructure does it little differently. Over the next few pages, I'll give you examples of some typical designs.

We will consider how we would cable or equip sites of different sizes. The standards suggest a minimum of two telecommunications outlets (TOs) per individual work area. The Institutes minimum was two TOs per person plus one between each person for a printer in a shared office. For administrative staff, the ratio was higher.

